      "reasoning": "I need to decide whether to mulligan down to 6 cards. Let me analyze my hand:\n\
\n\
1. **Boseiju, Who Endures** - Good land, can destroy artifacts/enchantments/nonbasic lands\n\
2. **Devourer of Destiny** - 6/6 colorless creature with cast ability that exiles a permanent and has a reveal ability for card selection\n\
3. **Eldrazi Temple** - Colorless land that can produce 2 colorless mana for Eldrazi spells\n\
4. **Forest** - Basic green land\n\
5. **Glaring Fleshraker** - 2/2 colorless creature that creates Eldrazi Spawn tokens and deals damage when colorless creatures enter\n\
6. **Kozilek's Command** - X spell that can do multiple things (token generation, scry/draw, exile creature, exile graveyard)\n\
7. **Ugin's Labyrinth** - Special land that can exile a colorless card with MV 7+ from hand to produce extra colorless mana\n\
\n\
This is an Eldrazi deck. I have good colorless spells and lands that support the theme. Devourer of Destiny has MV 7, which works with Ugin's Labyrinth. I have good mana sources (2 colorless lands that can produce extra mana, plus a Forest and Boseiju for green mana). The hand seems decent - I have a 6-drop, a 2-drop, and two lands that can produce extra mana. The Forest and Boseiju provide green mana if needed.\n\
\n\
The hand looks functional. I should keep it. Let me say no to the mulligan.",
