      "reasoning": "Now I'm in postcombat main phase. Opponent is at 13 life (they took 5 damage: 3 from combat, 1 from each Orcish Bowmasters trigger). Good!\n\
\n\
I have:\n\
- Mountain untapped (R)\n\
- 2 Blood Crypts tapped\n\
- Eldrazi Spawn token that can be sacrificed for {C}\n\
- 2 Orcish Bowmasters (1 tapped from attacking, 1 untapped)\n\
- Marauding Mako (tapped)\n\
- Orc Army Token (2/2 tapped)\n\
\n\
I can cast Burning Inquiry (R) or Street Wraith (3BB). Street Wraith needs BB plus 3 more, which I don't have. Burning Inquiry costs R which I have from Mountain.\n\
\n\
**Should I cast Burning Inquiry?**\n\
Pros:\n\
- Draws me 3 cards, discards 3 random\n\
- Could trigger Marauding Mako growth (gets +1/+1 counters for each card I discard)\n\
- Might disrupt opponent's hand\n\
\n\
Cons:\n\
- Could discard my good cards (Street Wraith, Bloodstained Mire)\n\
- Could give opponent good cards\n\
\n\
I have Orcish Bowmasters on board - if opponent draws extra cards from Burning Inquiry, my Orcish Bowmasters will trigger and deal 1 damage to any target for each card drawn beyond the first! Actually Burning Inquiry makes each player draw 3 cards. That's 3 draws for opponent, which triggers Orcish Bowmasters twice (for the 2nd and 3rd draws). So I'd get 2 triggers of 1 damage each, plus amass Orcs 1 each time. That's 2 more damage to opponent and 2 more +1/+1 counters on my Orc Army Token!\n\
\n\
Actually wait, Burning Inquiry draws 3 cards THEN discards 3 cards. So opponent would draw 3 cards, triggering Orcish Bowmasters twice (cards 2 and 3). That's 2 damage to any target and amass 1 twice.\n\
\n\
Then Marauding Mako would get +1/+1 counters for cards I discard (3 cards).\n\
\n\
This seems good! I should cast Burning Inquiry.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Burning Inquiry:\n\
