  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Mulliganed a strong 7-card hand with two lands, excellent curve (turn 1 Mako, turn 2 Bowmasters/Nethergoyf), free cycling from Street Wraith for card advantage and synergy. This hand has everything: mana, threats, interaction, and synergy.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. It has a perfect curve with Marauding Mako on turn 1, Orcish Bowmasters or Nethergoyf on turn 2, two lands including a fetchland, and Street Wraith for free cycling/card draw.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 1,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Put Hollow One on the bottom of the library instead of a redundant land, destroying the Turn 1 Burning Inquiry + free Hollow One combo. With Mountain + Burning Inquiry, casting Burning Inquiry discards 3 cards, reducing Hollow One's cost by 6 (making it free). This is one of the most powerful openings in the deck.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed Hollow One, keeping three lands",
      "better_line": "Bottom Bloodstained Mire (or Blood Crypt), keeping the Burning Inquiry + Hollow One + Marauding Mako package with Mountain to cast Burning Inquiry turn 1 for a free 4/4 and a growing Mako.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Blood Crypt directly instead of a Bloodstained Mire. Fetching with Mire first provides deck thinning and preserves the dual land in hand for a future turn where it could enter tapped if life is tight. The fetch can still find Blood Crypt untapped for the same color access this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played Blood Crypt directly from hand",
      "better_line": "Play Bloodstained Mire, sacrifice it to fetch Blood Crypt (or a basic Mountain/Swamp) untapped, preserving the other Blood Crypt in hand for later flexibility and gaining deck thinning.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 17,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 9,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Boseiju instead of Eldrazi Temple misses the opportunity to have 4 mana for Eldrazi spells this turn. With Eldrazi Temple, MiMo could cast Glaring Fleshraker (3 mana) and then Walking Ballista for X=0 (free colorless spell that triggers Fleshraker to create a Spawn token and deal 1 damage), generating more value this turn. Boseiju's channel ability isn't needed right now.",
      "action_taken": "Played Boseiju, Who Endures, producing only 3 total mana (2 colorless + 1 green)",
      "better_line": "Play Eldrazi Temple for 4 Eldrazi mana total, cast Glaring Fleshraker, then cast Walking Ballista X=0 to trigger Fleshraker (creating a Spawn token and dealing 1 damage)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 28,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decision_index": 14,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Returned Devourer of Destiny from Ugin's Labyrinth to hand instead of tapping for {C}{C}. This degrades the Labyrinth from producing 2 mana to 1 mana per turn, and the returned Devourer costs 7 mana which is many turns away from castable. More importantly, tapping for {C}{C} plus playing Eldrazi Temple and tapping Boseiju would have provided exactly enough mana to cast Glaring Fleshraker this turn, which is a key synergy piece.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Ugin's Labyrinth to return exiled Devourer of Destiny to hand",
      "better_line": "Tap Ugin's Labyrinth for {C}{C}, then in postcombat main play Eldrazi Temple, tap Boseiju for {G} and Eldrazi Temple for {C}, and cast Glaring Fleshraker for {2}{C}",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 31,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Bloodstained Mire instead of Mountain costs 1 life unnecessarily. With Blood Crypt already on board, playing Mountain provides the same mana access (1 generic + B from Blood Crypt = Orcish Bowmasters, or R from either land = Burning Inquiry) without needing to crack a fetch. The fetchlands are better saved for later turns when specific color fixing might be needed.",
      "action_taken": "Played Bloodstained Mire as the land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Mountain to save 1 life and preserve fetchlands for future turns when color fixing is more relevant",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 38,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to attack with Marauding Mako (1/1) into an empty board with no untapped mana on the opponent's side. The opponent has no blockers and no mana available to cast anything, so this is completely free damage.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and did not declare any attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Marauding Mako for 1 free damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 41,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 19,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetching Blood Crypt instead of Mountain means paying 2 life unnecessarily (or having it enter tapped). With Blood Crypt already in play providing black mana, and a Mountain already in hand for future turns, fetching Mountain here gets an untapped land for free while preserving 2 life points.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Blood Crypt (will cost 2 life to enter untapped or enter tapped)",
      "better_line": "Fetch Mountain - enters untapped for free, provides the generic mana needed for Orcish Bowmasters alongside existing Blood Crypt, and saves 2 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 47,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 22,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Timed out and declared no attackers when the opponent had no blockers and all lands tapped. This was a free 3 damage (Marauding Mako, Orcish Bowmasters, and Orc Army Token are all 1/1s) with essentially zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timeout) — no attackers declared.",
      "better_line": "Attack with at least Marauding Mako, Orcish Bowmasters, and Orc Army Token for 3 free damage, bringing opponent from 18 to 15.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 79,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 33,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "DSV3 Lucky targeted their own Marauding Mako (1/1) with an Orcish Bowmasters trigger, killing it for no benefit. The Mako could grow with future discard effects and was a useful creature. Meanwhile, the 1 damage could have gone to the opponent (bringing them closer to lethal range) or to an opponent's creature if relevant.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted own Marauding Mako 1/1 with Orcish Bowmasters' 1 damage trigger, killing it",
      "better_line": "Target the opponent (MiMo Rookie) with the Bowmasters trigger for 1 additional damage, preserving Marauding Mako as a threat that could grow from future discard effects",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Walking Ballista but couldn't complete mana payment, wasting a priority window in a critical turn. At 10 life facing 12+ power on the opponent's board, every action matters. The player should have first played Urza's Saga as their land drop to maximize available mana, then used their mana efficiently for Kozilek's Command (to exile a threat or create blockers) and/or Haywire Mite.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Walking Ballista, which was rolled back due to inability to pay mana costs.",
      "better_line": "Play Urza's Saga first (land drop), then cast Haywire Mite for {1} as a blocker, and cast Kozilek's Command using Eldrazi Temple + Ugin's Labyrinth mana to exile a key threat like the 8/8 Orc Army token or create Spawn blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 128,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decision_index": 45,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Activated Ugin's Labyrinth to return exiled Devourer of Destiny to hand in response to Thoughtseize. This gives the opponent an additional high-value target to choose with Thoughtseize, and permanently downgrades Ugin's Labyrinth from producing CC to just C. Meanwhile, casting Kozilek's Command in response (X=2 using Ugin's Labyrinth CC + Eldrazi Temple CC) could have exiled an Orcish Bowmasters (mana value 2) and provided card selection/draw, gaining real board advantage before Thoughtseize resolves.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Ugin's Labyrinth to return Devourer of Destiny to hand before Thoughtseize resolves.",
      "better_line": "Cast Kozilek's Command for X=2 in response to Thoughtseize, choosing to exile an Orcish Bowmasters (mana value 2) and scry 2 + draw a card. This removes a threat, generates card advantage, and the Command is spent before Thoughtseize resolves so it can't be taken.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 149,
      "player": "MiMo Rookie",
      "decision_index": 53,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Took Walking Ballista with Thoughtseize when the opponent can't cast a meaningful Ballista with only 3 lands. Devourer of Destiny is the real threat - it exiles a colored permanent on cast and could remove the 8/8 Orc Army token. With Eldrazi Temple + Ugin's Labyrinth (exiled card) + Boseiju, the opponent could reach 7 mana for Devourer relatively soon, while DSV3 Lucky is threatening lethal next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Took Walking Ballista with Thoughtseize",
      "better_line": "Take Devourer of Destiny, which is the most realistic way for the opponent to survive by exiling the 8/8 Orc Army token. Kozilek's Command is also a reasonable consideration as it's an instant-speed answer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 151,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 54,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Failed to declare attackers when the opponent is at 7 life with no blockers and no untapped mana. Any combination of attackers totaling 7+ power (e.g., the 8/8 Orc Army Token alone) would have been lethal. The opponent has no creatures and all lands are tapped.",
      "action_taken": "No response - failed to declare any attackers, missing guaranteed lethal.",
      "better_line": "Attack with all creatures (or at minimum the 8/8 Orc Army Token) for lethal damage against the opponent at 7 life with no blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 170,
      "player": "DSV3 Lucky",
      "decision_index": 62,
    }
  ],
